<title>USA: MBIA qualifies 13 issues for bond insurance.</title>
<headline>MBIA qualifies 13 issues for bond insurance.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>MBIA Insurance Co. said it has qualified for bond insurance the following 13 municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today.</p>
<p>--Jefferson UHSD, Calif., $6 million general obligation bonds, elective.</p>
<p>--Florida $160.655 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Bedford Community SD, Iowa, $2.1 million school GOs.</p>
<p>--Waterloo, Iowa, $4 million sewer revs is a direct purchase.</p>
<p>--Lewiston, Maine, $3.070 million public improvement GOs.</p>
<p>--Albion, Mich., $1.7 million GOs and 1.8 million water and sewer revs are a direct purchase</p>
<p>--Addison CSD, N.Y., $1.975 million school district bonds.</p>
<p>--Geneva City SD, N.Y., $6.5 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Seneca Falls CSD, N.Y., $1.3 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Spartanburg County SD#5, S.C., $4.1 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Austin, Texas, $18.4 million tax bonds</p>
<p>--North Texas Muni Water, Texas, $7.125 million revenue bonds.</p>
<p>((--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650))</p>
